#: ../../source/digital_thread/introduction.rst:60
msgid ""
"Because every phase is written into one declaration, nothing is copied from "
"one phase to the next, and nothing can fall out of step: the mass a "
"requirement is checked against is the mass ``pc info`` reports, worked out "
"from the same solid and the same material the bill of materials orders; the "
"bracket the instructions tell somebody to bolt on is the bracket that was "
"analysed. Changing the design is changing the one record, and every answer "
"that depended on it is asked again."
msgstr ""
"由于每一个阶段都写进同一份声明，所以没有任何东西要从一个阶段复制到下一个阶段，也没有任何东西会步调不一致：某项需求所对照的那个质量，就是 ``pc "
"info`` "
"报告的那个质量，它是由物料清单所订购的同一个实体和同一种材料算出来的；装配说明叫人用螺栓装上去的那个支架，就是被分析过的那个支架。改设计就是在改那一份记录，而每一个曾依赖它的答案都会被重新问一遍。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/introduction.rst:67
msgid ""
"One thing is deliberately left out of the package: which of the things that "
"can be either built or bought a particular person chooses to build (**Build "
"vs Buy**). The package says what can be bought and how what can be made is "
"made; the choice between them is a decision about who has which machines, "
"and is kept on the machine of whoever made it. A checkout does not carry it,"
" so the build plan and the order that follow from it can differ from one "
"person to the next while the product they describe does not."
msgstr ""
"有一样东西被有意地留在包之外：在那些既可以自制也可以采购的东西当中，某个特定的人选择自制哪些（**Build vs "
"Buy**）。包说明的是什么可以采购，以及可以自制的东西是怎么做的；而在两者之间作出选择，是一项关于谁手上有哪些机床的决定，它保存在做出它的那个人的机器上。一次检出并不会带着它，所以由它导出的构建计划和订单可以因人而异，而它们所描述的那个产品却不会。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/introduction.rst:76
msgid "Every answer is computed, not stored"
msgstr "每一个答案都是算出来的，而不是存下来的"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/introduction.rst:78
msgid ""
"What PartCAD says about an object -- a picture, a mass, a bill of materials,"
" a verdict -- is worked out from the declaration when it is asked for, and "
"cached under a key made of everything the answer depends on (see "
":ref:`caching`). A cached answer is never stale: change what it depends on "
"and the key changes with it. That is what lets one record serve every phase "
"without anybody having to remember to regenerate anything."
msgstr ""
"PartCAD 关于某个对象所说的东西 -- 一张图片、一个质量、一份物料清单、一个结论 -- "
"都是在被问到时从声明里算出来的，并按一个由该答案所依赖的一切内容构成的键来缓存（参见 :ref:`caching` "
"）。缓存下来的答案绝不会过期：改变它所依赖的东西，键也随之改变。正是这一点让同一份记录可以服务于每一个阶段，而不需要任何人记着去重新生成什么。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/introduction.rst:86
msgid "Every claim can be checked"
msgstr "每一条断言都可以被检查"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/introduction.rst:88
msgid ""
"A declaration states claims: this part is made by laser cutting, this "
"assembly's parts do not overlap, this mass is under 50 grams, this robot "
"does not tip over. ``pc test`` checks every claim that can be measured, ``pc"
" sim`` every claim about behaviour that a simulation can show, and the "
"``/pc:validate`` agent skill judges the rest from evidence it gathers and "
"names. See :doc:`/digital_thread/lifecycle/validation`."
msgstr ""
"声明会陈述各种断言：这个零件是用激光切割做出来的、这个装配体的零件之间不重叠、这个质量在 50 克以下、这台机器人不会倾倒。``pc test`` "
"检查每一条可测量的断言，``pc sim`` 检查每一条仿真能够显示的关于行为的断言，而 ``/pc:validate`` "
"智能体技能则依据它所收集并指明的证据来判定其余部分。参见 :doc:`/digital_thread/lifecycle/validation` 。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/introduction.rst:95
msgid "Packages build on packages"
msgstr "包建立在包之上"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/introduction.rst:97
msgid ""
"A package imports others -- standard fasteners, a supplier's catalogue, a "
"colleague's sub-assembly -- and uses their objects by name "
"(``//pub/std/...``). The thread of a product runs through every package it "
"is made of: the screw's interface is the screw package's, its supplier is "
"the supplier's, and both are read where they are declared rather than copied"
" in."
msgstr ""
"一个包会导入其他包 -- 标准紧固件、某个供应商的目录册、某位同事的子装配体 -- 并按名称使用它们的对象（ ``//pub/std/...`` "
"）。一个产品的主线贯穿它所由之构成的每一个包：螺钉的接口属于螺钉那个包，它的供应商属于供应商那个包，而两者都是在它们被声明的地方读取的，而不是被复制进来的。"
